<title>UK: Delta says to cut about 90 jobs.</title>
<headline>Delta says to cut about 90 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British cable manufacturer Delta Plc said on Thursday it was launching a second restructuring project which would lead to 90 redundancies.</p>
<p>Delta said it decided to close its wire mill at Brimsdown after it lost a major contract in its copper wire operation. It said it was aiming to develop Enfield Winding Wires as a self-sufficient business unit.</p>
<p>Delta said it launched its first restructuring project in September 1995 at a cost of 11 million pounds.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
